# Configuración in Idoneo apps

App-specific settings belong on a **`/settings` page**, same pattern as Assistant and Ads.

- **UserMenu** (team managers only): `Link` to `/settings` labeled **Configuración** with `SettingsIcon`.
- Do **not** add a one-off menu item (e.g. Remitente) that opens a modal.
- Banners and “configure here” links go to `/settings`, not `openModal()`.
- Protect the route: if the user cannot manage the team, redirect to `/profile`.

```tsx
// ✅ DO
<Link role="menuitem" href="/settings" onClick={() => setOpen(false)}>
  <SettingsIcon className="h-4 w-4 text-[var(--muted)]" />
  Configuración
</Link>

// ❌ DON'T
<button type="button" onClick={() => { setOpen(false); openSenderConfig() }}>
  Remitente
</button>
```

The settings page title is **Configuración**. Put product settings there (Mailer sender, Ads connections, Assistant prompts, etc.). Profile and Negocio stay on `/profile` and `/business`.
